<title>SPAIN: BASKETBALL-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>BASKETBALL-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>GERONA, Spain 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results in the European</p>
<p>basketball championship on Monday:</p>
<p>Second round</p>
<p>Group E (in Gerona)</p>
<p>Israel 69 Russia 87 (halftime 31-43)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Israel - Oded Katash 14, Gur Shelef 14, Nadav Henefeld 11,</p>
<p>Tomer Steinhauer 10.</p>
<p>Russia - Andrei Fetissov 16, Vassily Karassev 14, Igor</p>
<p>Koudelin 11, Sergei Babkov 11, Sergei Panov 9.</p>
<p>Group F (in Badalona)</p>
<p>Germany 62 Italy 67 (28-27)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Germany - Henrik Roedl 20, Denis Wucherer 14, Patrick</p>
<p>Femerling 10.</p>
<p>Italy - Carlton Myers 13, Gregor Fucka 13, Davide Bonora 11,</p>
<p>Giacomo Galanda 9.</p>
<p>Places 13-16 (played in Badalona):</p>
<p>Bosnia 96 Latvia 94 (32-52)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Bosnia - Nenad Markovic 44, Dzevad Alihodzic 13, Samir Avdic</p>
<p>12, Aris Beciragic 8, Samir Seleskovic 8.</p>
<p>Latvia - Ainars Bagatskis 33, Raimonds Miglinieks 18,</p>
<p>Roberts Stelmahers 16, Uvis Helmanis 11.</p>
<p>Slovenia 75 Ukraine 80 (46-45)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Slovenia - Marko Milic 16, Jurij Zdovc 14, Radosav</p>
<p>Nesterovic 12, Marko Tusek 12, Ivica Jurkovic 10.</p>
<p>Ukraine - Oleksander Okunski 18, Yevgeny Murzine 13, Igor</p>
<p>Molchanov 9, Grigory Khizhnyak 9, Oleksander Lokhmanchuk 9.</p>
<p>Final placings:</p>
<p>13. Ukraine</p>
<p>14. Slovenia</p>
<p>15. Bosnia</p>
<p>16. Latvia</p>
<p>Group E (in Gerona) France 71 Greece 80 (33-37)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>France - Yann Bonato 16, Fabien Dubos 12, Remi Rippert 12, Laurent Foirest 9, Frederic Fauthoux 8.</p>
<p>Greece - Fragiskos Alvertis 17, Nikos Ekonomou 16, Demetrios Papanikolaou 9, Efthimios Rentzias 9, Theofanis Christodolou 8. Spain 104 Poland 61 (52-29)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Spain - Alfonso Reyes 21, Alberto Angulo 21, Ferrran Martinez 15, Roberto Duenas 12, Antonio Paraiso 8.</p>
<p>Poland - Maciej Zielinksi 10, Adam Wojcik 10, Rafal Bigus 7.</p>
